module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Fischer.AtlasCarriers.Fi22TransvectionComparison.Generation.Edges.FamilyA
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Fischer.AtlasCarriers.Fi22TransvectionComparison.Generation.Edges.FamilyB

/-!
# Fi22 Schreier-edge membership

Both defining ATLAS generators have all their literal Schreier edges in the
subgroup generated by conjugates commuting with A. The certificate uses the six
previously certified seeds, nine additional products of those seeds, and the
faithful 48-coordinate test. BFS tree edges are discharged by cancellation.

This is exactly the remaining premise of
`exists_commutingConjugate_certificate_of_edges` in `Generation.lean`.
The unconditional generation and coverage assembly stays in that module.

Source: ATLAS F22G1-p3510B0 and the conjugation-action paragraph following GLS3
Table 5.3t in `refs/KGroup/GLS3/Chapter5(sec3-).tex`.
-/

public section
namespace Sporadic.Fischer.Fi22.TransvectionComparison

/-- The complete edge-membership premise for the actual Fi22 commuting-conjugate certificate. -/
theorem schreierEdge_mem_commutingConjugateSubgroup :
    ∀ s ∈ atlasGenerators, ∀ x : Fin 3510,
      (pointTransport (inclusion s x))⁻¹ * s * pointTransport x ∈
        commutingConjugateSubgroup := by
  intro s hs x
  change s = atlasA ∨ s = atlasB at hs
  rcases hs with rfl | rfl
  · exact atlasA_schreierEdge_mem x
  · exact atlasB_schreierEdge_mem x

end Sporadic.Fischer.Fi22.TransvectionComparison
